  "notes": "Installed PyOpenGL and mapbox-vector-tile into both venvs; apt-installed libpulse0, xvfb and Qt's X11/xcb libraries. The workload starts its own Xvfb display (unix socket only, software Mesa OpenGL, no GPU) and builds the iPhotos.src/iPhotos.maps package layout under /tmp/kt_140: src is a symlink to the code under test, maps is a copy with an empty tiles dir so MainWindow can start. It drives the real MainWindow -> EditController.begin_edit -> image load -> sidebar preview flow on 5 generated images. It also calls _start_sidebar_preview_preparation directly with 2 full-resolution frames and runs EditSidebarPreviewWorker on the main thread with target_height 320 and -1 (repo-test style). Qt thread-pool workers do the real image loading and preview work. Head coverage 0.804 (115/143), base 1.0 (7/7). Digests differ by design: head computes sidebar stats from the GPU-scaled preview, and target_height -1 means pass-through on head but a 64 px scale on base. Each side's digest is the same across repeated runs."
